re dots (灬) — hot' },\n        '冷': { components: ['冫','令'], radical: '冫', explanation: 'Ice (冫) + command (令) — cold' },\n        '新': { components: ['亲','斤'], radical: '斤', explanation: 'Close (亲) + axe (斤) — new' },\n        '旧': { components: ['丨','日'], radical: '日', explanation: 'Stroke + sun (日) — old/used' },\n        '春': { components: ['三','人','日'], radical: '日', explanation: 'Three + person + sun — spring' },\n        '夏': { components: ['一','自','夊'], radical: '夊', explanation: 'Self under sun + walking — summer' },\n        '秋': { components: ['禾','火'], radical: '禾', explanation: 'Grain (禾) + fire (火) — autumn harvest' },\n        '冬': { components: ['夂','冫'], radical: '冫', explanation: 'Descend (夂) + ice (冫) — winter' },\n        '快': { components: ['忄','夬'], radical: '忄', explanation: 'Heart (忄) + decisive (夬) — fast/happy' },\n        '慢': { components: ['忄','曼'], radical: '忄', explanation: 'Heart (忄) + prolonged (曼) — slow' },\n        '难': { components: ['又','隹'], radical: '隹', explanation: 'Again (又) + short-tailed bird (隹) — difficult' },\n        '忙': { components: ['忄','亡'], radical: '忄', explanation: 'Heart (忄) + perish (亡) — busy' },\n        '教': { components: ['孝','攵'], radical: '攵', explanation: 'Filial piety (孝) + strike (攵) — to teach' },\n        '问': { components: ['门','口'], radical: '门', explanation: 'Door (门) + mouth (口) — to ask' },\n        '答': { components: ['竹','合'], radical: '竹', explanation: 'Bamboo (竹) + join (合) — to answer' },\n        '给': { components: ['纟','合'], radical: '纟', explanation: 'Silk (纟) + join (合) — to give' },\n        '找': { components: ['扌','戈'], radical: '扌', explanation: 'Hand (扌) + halberd (戈) — to find' },\n        '帮': { components: ['邦','巾'], radical: '巾', explanation: 'Country (邦) + cloth (巾) — to help' },\n        '等': { components: ['竹','寺'], radical: '竹', explanation: 'Bamboo (竹) + temple (寺) — to wait' },\n        '穿': { components: ['穴','牙'], radical: '穴', explanation: 'Cave (穴) + tooth (牙) — to wear/pierce' },\n        '洗': { components: ['氵','先'], radical: '氵', explanation: 'Water (氵) + first (先) — to wash' },\n        '记': { components: ['讠','己'], radical: '讠', explanation: 'Words (讠) + self (己) — to remember' },\n        '忘': { components: ['亡','心'], radical: '心', explanation: 'Perish (亡) + heart (心) — to forget' },\n        '玩': { components: ['王','元'], radical: '王', explanation: 'Jade (王) + origin (元) — to play' },\n        '笑': { components: ['竹','夭'], radical: '竹', explanation: 'Bamboo (竹) + young (夭) — to laugh' },\n        '哭': { components: ['口','口','犬'], radical: '口', explanation: 'Two mouths + dog — to cry' },\n        '见': { components: ['见'], radical: '见', explanation: 'Simplified from 見 — to see' },\n        '借': { components: ['亻','昔'], radical: '亻', explanation: 'Person (亻) + old times (昔) — to borrow' },\n        '还': { components: ['辶','不'], radical: '辶', explanation: 'Walk (辶) + not (不) — to return' },\n        '病': { components: ['疒','丙'], radical: '疒', explanation: 'Illness (疒) + third (丙) — sick' },\n        '云': { components: ['二','厶'], radical: '二', explanation: 'Simplified from 雲 — cloud' },\n        '河': { components: ['氵','可'], radical: '氵', explanation: 'Water (氵) + can (可) — river' },\n        '海': { components: ['氵','每'], radical: '氵', explanation: 'Water (氵) + every (每) — sea/ocean' },\n        '石': { components: ['石'], radical: '石', explanation: 'Pictograph of a stone/cliff' },\n        '光': { components: ['⺌','儿'], radical: '儿', explanation: 'Fire above legs (儿) — light' },\n        '星': { components: ['日','生'], radical: '日', explanation: 'Sun (日) + birth (生) — star' },\n        '草': { components: ['艹','早'], radical: '艹', explanation: 'Grass (艹) + early (早) — grass' },\n        '用': { components: ['用'], radical: '用', explanation: 'Pictograph of a bucket — to use' },\n        '朋': { components: ['月','月'], radical: '月', explanation: 'Two moons (月月) — friend' },\n        '友': { components: ['又'], radical: '又', explanation: 'Two right hands clasped — friend' },\n        '老': { components: ['耂','匕'], radical: '耂', explanation: 'Old person + spoon — old/teacher' },\n        '师': { components: ['丨','帅'], radical: '巾', explanation: 'Simplified from 師 — teacher/master' },\n        '父': { components: ['八','乂'], radical: '父', explanation: 'Hand holding a stone axe — father' },\n        '母': { components: ['母'], radical: '母', explanation: 'Pictograph of a mother nursing' }\n    };\n\n    // ===== Feature 6: Example Sentences =====\n    const exampleSentences = {\n        '学': [\n            { chinese: '我在学中文。', pinyin: 'Wǒ zài xué zhōngwén.', english: 'I am studying Chinese.' },\n            { chinese: '学生们很努力。', pinyin: 'Xuéshēngmen hěn nǔlì.', english: 'The students work very hard.' }\n        ],\n        '说': [\n            { chinese: '请你说慢一点。', pinyin: 'Qǐng nǐ shuō màn yīdiǎn.', english: 'Please speak more slowly.' },\n            { chinese: '他会说三种语言。', pinyin: 'Tā huì shuō sān zhǒng yǔyán.', english: 'He can speak three languages.' }\n        ],\n        '看': [\n            { chinese: '我在看书。', pinyin: 'Wǒ zài kàn shū.', english: 'I am reading a book.' },\n            { chinese: '你看那个！', pinyin: 'Nǐ kàn nàge!', english: 'Look at that!' }\n        ],\n        '来': [\n            { chinese: '你来这里。', pinyin: 'Nǐ lái zhèlǐ.', english: 'Come here.' },\n            { chinese: '他从中国来。', pinyin: 'Tā cóng Zhōngguó lái.', english: 'He comes from China.' }\n        ],\n        '去': [\n            { chinese: '我去学校。', pinyin: 'Wǒ qù xuéxiào.', english: 'I go to school.' },\n            { chinese: '你想去哪儿？', pinyin: 'Nǐ xiǎng qù nǎr?', english: 'Where do you want to go?' }\n        ],\n        '吃': [\n            { chinese: '我们吃饭吧。', pinyin: 'Wǒmen chīfàn ba.', english: \"Let's eat.\" },\n            { chinese: '你吃早饭了吗？', pinyin: 'Nǐ chī zǎofàn le ma?', english: 'Did you eat breakfast?' }\n        ],\n        '喝': [\n            { chinese: '我想喝水。', pinyin: 'Wǒ xiǎng hē shuǐ.', english: 'I want to drink water.' },\n            { chinese: '你喝茶还是咖啡？', pinyin: 'Nǐ hē chá háishì kāfēi?', english: 'Do you drink tea or coffee?' }\n        ],\n        '做': [\n            { chinese: '你在做什么？', pinyin: 'Nǐ zài zuò shénme?', english: 'What are you doing?' },\n            { chinese: '她做得很好。', pinyin: 'Tā zuò de hěn hǎo.', english: 'She did very well.' }\n        ],\n        '好': [\n            { chinese: '你好！', pinyin: 'Nǐ hǎo!', english: 'Hello!' },\n            { chinese: '这个很好吃。', pinyin: 'Zhège hěn hǎochī.', english: 'This is very delicious.' }\n        ],\n        '大': [\n            { chinese: '这个房间很大。', pinyin: 'Zhège fángjiān hěn dà.', english: 'This room is very big.' }\n        ],\n        '小': [\n            { chinese: '她有一只小猫。', pinyin: 'Tā yǒu yī zhī xiǎo māo.', english: 'She has a small cat.' }\n        ],\n        '水': [\n            { chinese: '请给我一杯水。', pinyin: 'Qǐng gěi wǒ yī bēi shuǐ.', english: 'Please give me a glass of water.' }\n        ],\n        '火': [\n            { chinese: '小心火！', pinyin: 'Xiǎoxīn huǒ!', english: 'Be careful of fire!' }\n        ],\n        '山': [\n            { chinese: '那座山很高。', pinyin: 'Nà zuò shān hěn gāo.', english: 'That mountain is very tall.' }\n        ],\n        '天': [\n            { chinese: '今天天气很好。', pinyin: 'Jīntiān tiānqì hěn hǎo.', english: 'The weather is very nice today.' }\n        ],\n        '人': [\n            { chinese: '那个人是谁？', pinyin: 'Nàge rén shì shéi?', english: 'Who is that person?' }\n        ],\n        '想': [\n            { chinese: '我想你了。', pinyin: 'Wǒ xiǎng nǐ le.', english: 'I miss you.' },\n            { chinese: '你想吃什么？', pinyin: 'Nǐ xiǎng chī shénme?', english: 'What do you want to eat?' }\n        ],\n        '知': [\n            { chinese: '我不知道。', pinyin: 'Wǒ bù zhīdào.', english: \"I don't know.\" }\n        ],\n        '听': [\n            { chinese: '请听我说。', pinyin: 'Qǐng tīng wǒ shuō.', english: 'Please listen to me.' }\n        ],\n        '读': [\n            { chinese: '我每天读中文。', pinyin: 'Wǒ měitiān dú zhōngwén.', english: 'I read Chinese every day.' }\n        ],\n        '写': [\n            { chinese: '你会写汉字吗？', pinyin: 'Nǐ huì xiě hànzì ma?', english: 'Can you write Chinese characters?' }\n        ],\n        '买': [\n            { chinese: '我要买东西。', pinyin: 'Wǒ yào mǎi dōngxi.', english: 'I want to buy things.' }\n        ],\n        '卖': [\n            { chinese: '他卖水果。', pinyin: 'Tā mài shuǐguǒ.', english: 'He sells fruit.' }\n        ],\n        '走': [\n            { chinese: '我们走吧。', pinyin: 'Wǒmen zǒu ba.', english: \"Let's go.\" }\n        ],\n        '跑': [\n            { chinese: '他跑得很快。', pinyin: 'Tā pǎo de hěn kuài.', english: 'He runs very fast.' }\n        ],\n        '快': [\n            { chinese: '快点！', pinyin: 'Kuài diǎn!', english: 'Hurry up!' },\n            { chinese: '时间过得很快。', pinyin: 'Shíjiān guò de hěn kuài.', english: 'Time passes very quickly.' }\n        ],\n        '慢': [\n            { chinese: '请慢慢走。', pinyin: 'Qǐng mànmàn zǒu.', english: 'Please walk slowly.' }\n        ],\n        '高': [\n            { chinese: '他很高。', pinyin: 'Tā hěn gāo.', english: 'He is very tall.' }\n        ],\n        '爱': [\n            { chinese: '我爱你。', pinyin: 'Wǒ ài nǐ.', english: 'I love you.' },\n            { chinese: '她爱唱歌。', pinyin: 'Tā ài chànggē.', english: 'She loves to sing.' }\n        ],\n        '教': [\n            { chinese: '她教我中文。', pinyin: 'Tā jiāo wǒ zhōngwén.', english: 'She teaches me Chinese.' }\n        ],\n        '问': [\n            { chinese: '我想问你一个问题。', pinyin: 'Wǒ xiǎng wèn nǐ yīge wèntí.', english: 'I want to ask you a question.' }\n        ],\n        '给': [\n            { chinese: '请给我看看。', pinyin: 'Qǐng gěi wǒ kànkan.', english: 'Please show me.' }\n        ],\n        '找': [\n            { chinese: '我在找钥匙。', pinyin: 'Wǒ zài zhǎo yàoshi.', english: 'I am looking for my keys.' }\n        ],\n        '等': [\n            { chinese: '请等一下。', pinyin: 'Qǐng děng yīxià.', english: 'Please wait a moment.' }\n        ],\n        '帮': [\n            { chinese: '你能帮我吗？', pinyin: 'Nǐ néng bāng wǒ ma?', english: 'Can you help me?' }\n        ],\n        '明': [\n            { chinese: '明天见！', pinyin: 'Míngtiān jiàn!', english: 'See you tomorrow!' }\n        ],\n        '花': [\n            { chinese: '这朵花很漂亮。', pinyin: 'Zhè duǒ huā hěn piàoliang.', english: 'This flower is very beautiful.' }\n        ],\n        '新': [\n            { chinese: '新年快乐！', pinyin: 'Xīnnián kuàilè!', english: 'Happy New Year!' }\n        ],\n        '热': [\n            { chinese: '今天很热。', pinyin: 'Jīntiān hěn rè.', english: 'It is very hot today.' }\n        ],\n        '冷': [\n            { chinese: '冬天很冷。', pinyin: 'Dōngtiān hěn lěng.', english: 'Winter is very cold.' }\n        ],\n        '难': [\n            { chinese: '中文很难学。', pinyin: 'Zhōngwén hěn nán xué.', english: 'Chinese is very hard to learn.' }\n        ],\n        '忙': [\n            { chinese: '你最近忙吗？', pinyin: 'Nǐ zuìjìn máng ma?', english: 'Have you been busy lately?' }\n        ],\n        '笑': [\n            { chinese: '她笑了。', pinyin: 'Tā xiào le.', english: 'She laughed.' }\n        ],\n        '哭': [\n            { chinese: '宝宝在哭。', pinyin: 'Bǎobao zài kū.', english: 'The baby is crying.' }\n        ],\n        '开': [\n            { chinese: '请开门。', pinyin: 'Qǐng kāi mén.', english: 'Please open the door.' }\n        ],\n        '关': [\n            { chinese: '请关窗户。', pinyin: 'Qǐng guān chuānghù.', english: 'Please close the window.' }\n        ],\n        '春': [\n            { chinese: '春天来了。', pinyin: 'Chūntiān lái le.', english: 'Spring has come.' }\n        ],\n        '冬': [\n            { chinese: '冬天下雪。', pinyin: 'Dōngtiān xià xuě.', english: 'It snows in winter.' }\n        ],\n        '男': [\n            { chinese: '他是一个男生。', pinyin: 'Tā shì yīge nánshēng.', english: 'He is a boy.' }\n        ],\n        '女': [\n            { chinese: '那个女孩很聪明。', pinyin: 'Nàge nǚhái hěn cōngmíng.', english: 'That girl is very smart.' }\n        ],\n        '朋': [\n            { chinese: '他是我的朋友。', pinyin: 'Tā shì wǒ de péngyǒu.', english: 'He is my friend.' }\n        ],\n        '老': [\n            { chinese: '我的老师很好。', pinyin: 'Wǒ de lǎoshī hěn hǎo.', english: 'My teacher is very good.' }\n        ],\n        '病': [\n            { chinese: '他生病了。', pinyin: 'Tā shēngbìng le.', english: 'He is sick.' }\n        ],\n        '雨': [\n            { chinese: '下雨了。', pinyin: 'Xià yǔ le.', english: 'It is raining.' }\n        ],\n        '雪': [\n            { chinese: '外面下雪了！', pinyin: 'Wàimiàn xià xuě le!', english: 'It is snowing outside!' }\n        ],\n        '风': [\n            { chinese: '今天风很大。', pinyin: 'Jīntiān fēng hěn dà.', english: 'The wind is strong today.' }\n        ],\n        '河': [\n            { chinese: '这条河很长。', pinyin: 'Zhè tiáo hé hěn cháng.', english: 'This river is very long.' }\n        ],\n        '海': [\n            { chinese: '我喜欢大海。', pinyin: 'Wǒ xǐhuan dàhǎi.', english: 'I like the ocean.' }\n        ]\n    };\n\n    // Curated list for Stroke Order Challenge - only characters with Hanzi Writer support\n    // These characters are guaranteed to have real stroke-by-stroke animation data\n    const strokeChallengeCharacters = [\n        { character: '人', pinyin: 'rén', meaning: 'person', strokes: 2 },\n        { character: '大', pinyin: 'dà', meaning: 'big', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '小', pinyin: 'xiǎo', meaning: 'small', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '中', pinyin: 'zhōng', meaning: 'middle', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '一', pinyin: 'yī', meaning: 'one', strokes: 1 },\n        { character: '二', pinyin: 'èr', meaning: 'two', strokes: 2 },\n        { character: '三', pinyin: 'sān', meaning: 'three', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '四', pinyin: 'sì', meaning: 'four', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '五', pinyin: 'wǔ', meaning: 'five', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '六', pinyin: 'liù', meaning: 'six', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '七', pinyin: 'qī', meaning: 'seven', strokes: 2 },\n        { character: '八', pinyin: 'bā', meaning: 'eight', strokes: 2 },\n        { character: '九', pinyin: 'jiǔ', meaning: 'nine', strokes: 2 },\n        { character: '十', pinyin: 'shí', meaning: 'ten', strokes: 2 },\n        { character: '山', pinyin: 'shān', meaning: 'mountain', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '水', pinyin: 'shuǐ', meaning: 'water', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '火', pinyin: 'huǒ', meaning: 'fire', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '木', pinyin: 'mù', meaning: 'wood', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '金', pinyin: 'jīn', meaning: 'gold', strokes: 8 },\n        { character: '土', pinyin: 'tǔ', meaning: 'earth', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '日', pinyin: 'rì', meaning: 'sun', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '月', pinyin: 'yuè', meaning: 'moon', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '年', pinyin: 'nián', meaning: 'year', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '天', pinyin: 'tiān', meaning: 'sky', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '手', pinyin: 'shǒu', meaning: 'hand', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '口', pinyin: 'kǒu', meaning: 'mouth', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '目', pinyin: 'mù', meaning: 'eye', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '心', pinyin: 'xīn', meaning: 'heart', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '女', pinyin: 'nǚ', meaning: 'woman', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '男', pinyin: 'nán', meaning: 'man', strokes: 7 },\n        { character: '子', pinyin: 'zǐ', meaning: 'child', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '好', pinyin: 'hǎo', meaning: 'good', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '吃', pinyin: 'chī', meaning: 'eat', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '坐', pinyin: 'zuò', meaning: 'sit', strokes: 7 },\n        { character: '上', pinyin: 'shàng', meaning: 'up', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '下', pinyin: 'xià', meaning: 'down', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '左', pinyin: 'zuǒ', meaning: 'left', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '右', pinyin: 'yòu', meaning: 'right', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '前', pinyin: 'qián', meaning: 'front', strokes: 9 },\n        { character: '后', pinyin: 'hòu', meaning: 'back', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '东', pinyin: 'dōng', meaning: 'east', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '西', pinyin: 'xī', meaning: 'west', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '南', pinyin: 'nán', meaning: 'south', strokes: 9 },\n        { character: '北', pinyin: 'běi', meaning: 'north', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '白', pinyin: 'bái', meaning: 'white', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '黑', pinyin: 'hēi', meaning: 'black', strokes: 12 },\n        { character: '红', pinyin: 'hóng', meaning: 'red', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '生', pinyin: 'shēng', meaning: 'life', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '字', pinyin: 'zì', meaning: 'character', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '本', pinyin: 'běn', meaning: 'book', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '车', pinyin: 'chē', meaning: 'car', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '门', pinyin: 'mén', meaning: 'door', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '马', pinyin: 'mǎ', meaning: 'horse', strokes: 3 },\n        { character: '牛', pinyin: 'niú', meaning: 'cow', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '羊', pinyin: 'yáng', meaning: 'sheep', strokes: 6 },\n        { character: '鱼', pinyin: 'yú', meaning: 'fish', strokes: 8 },\n        { character: '鸟', pinyin: 'niǎo', meaning: 'bird', strokes: 5 },\n        { character: '雨', pinyin: 'yǔ', meaning: 'rain', strokes: 8 },\n        { character: '风', pinyin: 'fēng', meaning: 'wind', strokes: 4 },\n        { character: '云', pinyin: 'yún', meaning: 'cloud', strokes: 4 }\n    ];\n\n    // Detailed radical information for interactive learning\n    const radicalsData = {\n        '人': {\n            character: '人',\n            alternateForms: ['亻'],\n            pinyin: 'rén',\n            meaning: 'person, human',\n            etymology: 'Originally depicted a person standing with legs apart. When used as a radical on the left side of characters, it transforms into 亻 (single person radical).',\n            positions: 'Appears on the left side (亻) or as a standalone character (人)',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '你', pinyin: 'nǐ', meaning: 'you', explanation: 'Person (亻) + you = informal \"you\"' },\n                { char: '他', pinyin: 'tā', meaning: 'he/him', explanation: 'Person (亻) + also = \"he\" (another person)' },\n                { char: '们', pinyin: 'men', meaning: 'plural marker', explanation: 'Person (亻) + gate = makes pronouns plural' },\n                { char: '什', pinyin: 'shén', meaning: 'what', explanation: 'Person (亻) + ten = used in 什么 (what)' },\n                { char: '休', pinyin: 'xiū', meaning: 'to rest', explanation: 'Person (亻) + tree = person leaning on tree to rest' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 亻 usually relate to people, human actions, or personal characteristics.'\n        },\n        '水': {\n            character: '水',\n            alternateForms: ['氵', '氺'],\n            pinyin: 'shuǐ',\n            meaning: 'water',\n            etymology: 'Ancient form depicted a flowing river. When used as a radical, it becomes 氵 (three drops) on the left side, representing liquids and water-related concepts.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 氵, or bottom as 氺, or standalone as 水',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '河', pinyin: 'hé', meaning: 'river', explanation: 'Water (氵) + can = flowing water, a river' },\n                { char: '海', pinyin: 'hǎi', meaning: 'sea/ocean', explanation: 'Water (氵) + every = vast water, the sea' },\n                { char: '洗', pinyin: 'xǐ', meaning: 'to wash', explanation: 'Water (氵) + before = to wash, cleanse with water' },\n                { char: '泪', pinyin: 'lèi', meaning: 'tears', explanation: 'Water (氵) + eye-related = water from eyes' },\n                { char: '湖', pinyin: 'hú', meaning: 'lake', explanation: 'Water (氵) + ancient = a body of water, lake' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Nearly all characters with 氵relate to water, liquids, or fluid-related actions.'\n        },\n        '心': {\n            character: '心',\n            alternateForms: ['忄', '㣺'],\n            pinyin: 'xīn',\n            meaning: 'heart, mind, emotion',\n            etymology: 'Depicts the physical shape of a heart. Represents emotions, thoughts, and psychological states. As a radical, often appears as 忄 on the left.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 忄, bottom as 心, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '想', pinyin: 'xiǎng', meaning: 'to think', explanation: 'Tree/eye + heart (心) = thoughts from the heart/mind' },\n                { char: '快', pinyin: 'kuài', meaning: 'fast/happy', explanation: 'Decide + heart (忄) = quick feelings, happiness' },\n                { char: '情', pinyin: 'qíng', meaning: 'emotion', explanation: 'Blue/green + heart (忄) = feelings, emotions' },\n                { char: '怕', pinyin: 'pà', meaning: 'to fear', explanation: 'White + heart (忄) = fear, to be afraid' },\n                { char: '慢', pinyin: 'màn', meaning: 'slow', explanation: 'Again + heart (忄) = relaxed pace, slow' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 忄 or 心 typically relate to emotions, mental states, or psychological concepts.'\n        },\n        '手': {\n            character: '手',\n            alternateForms: ['扌', '𠂇'],\n            pinyin: 'shǒu',\n            meaning: 'hand',\n            etymology: 'Depicts an open hand with fingers. As a radical (扌), represents hand actions and manual activities.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 扌, or standalone as 手',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '打', pinyin: 'dǎ', meaning: 'to hit', explanation: 'Hand (扌) + nail = to strike, hit with hand' },\n                { char: '拿', pinyin: 'ná', meaning: 'to take', explanation: 'Hand action (扌) + together = to grasp, take' },\n                { char: '推', pinyin: 'tuī', meaning: 'to push', explanation: 'Hand (扌) + bird = to push forward' },\n                { char: '拉', pinyin: 'lā', meaning: 'to pull', explanation: 'Hand (扌) + stand = to pull toward' },\n                { char: '扔', pinyin: 'rēng', meaning: 'to throw', explanation: 'Hand (扌) + force away = to toss, throw' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 扌 describe manual actions, hand movements, or things done with hands.'\n        },\n        '口': {\n            character: '口',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'kǒu',\n            meaning: 'mouth, opening',\n            etymology: 'A simple square representing an open mouth. Can represent speech, eating, or any opening.',\n            positions: 'Left side, bottom, or enclosing other components',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '吃', pinyin: 'chī', meaning: 'to eat', explanation: 'Mouth (口) + beg = to eat, consume food' },\n                { char: '喝', pinyin: 'hē', meaning: 'to drink', explanation: 'Mouth (口) + yawn = to drink liquids' },\n                { char: '叫', pinyin: 'jiào', meaning: 'to call', explanation: 'Mouth (口) + reach = to call out, shout' },\n                { char: '唱', pinyin: 'chàng', meaning: 'to sing', explanation: 'Mouth (口) + two mouths = singing, vocal music' },\n                { char: '吗', pinyin: 'ma', meaning: 'question', explanation: 'Mouth (口) + horse = question particle (sound)' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 口 relate to mouth actions (speaking, eating), sounds, or openings.'\n        },\n        '木': {\n            character: '木',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'mù',\n            meaning: 'tree, wood',\n            etymology: 'Pictograph of a tree with branches above and roots below. Represents wood, trees, and wooden objects.',\n            positions: 'Left side, bottom, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '林', pinyin: 'lín', meaning: 'forest', explanation: 'Two trees (木木) = a small forest, woods' },\n                { char: '树', pinyin: 'shù', meaning: 'tree', explanation: 'Wood (木) + to support = a standing tree' },\n                { char: '森', pinyin: 'sēn', meaning: 'dense forest', explanation: 'Three trees (木木木) = a thick forest' },\n                { char: '村', pinyin: 'cūn', meaning: 'village', explanation: 'Wood (木) + inch/foot = settlement near woods' },\n                { char: '板', pinyin: 'bǎn', meaning: 'board/plank', explanation: 'Wood (木) + reverse = flat wooden board' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 木 relate to trees, wood, wooden objects, or plant life.'\n        },\n        '日': {\n            character: '日',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'rì',\n            meaning: 'sun, day',\n            etymology: 'Originally a circle with a dot representing the sun. Later squared for easier writing.',\n            positions: 'Left side, top, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '明', pinyin: 'míng', meaning: 'bright', explanation: 'Sun (日) + moon (月) = brightness from both luminaries' },\n                { char: '时', pinyin: 'shí', meaning: 'time', explanation: 'Sun (日) + temple/earth = marking time by sun' },\n                { char: '晚', pinyin: 'wǎn', meaning: 'evening', explanation: 'Sun (日) + free = when sun sets, evening' },\n                { char: '早', pinyin: 'zǎo', meaning: 'early/morning', explanation: 'Sun (日) + ten = early in the day' },\n                { char: '晴', pinyin: 'qíng', meaning: 'clear weather', explanation: 'Sun (日) + blue = sunny, clear skies' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 日 relate to sun, time, daylight, or brightness.'\n        },\n        '月': {\n            character: '月',\n            alternateForms: ['⺼'],\n            pinyin: 'yuè',\n            meaning: 'moon, month / flesh',\n            etymology: 'Depicts a crescent moon. Also represents flesh/body parts when written as ⺼, as they looked similar in ancient forms.',\n            positions: 'Left side (often as body part radical ⺼), right side, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '明', pinyin: 'míng', meaning: 'bright', explanation: 'Sun (日) + moon (月) = combined brightness' },\n                { char: '期', pinyin: 'qī', meaning: 'period/date', explanation: 'Moon (月) + basis = time period, date' },\n                { char: '朋', pinyin: 'péng', meaning: 'friend', explanation: 'Two moons (月月) = friendship, companionship' },\n                { char: '肚', pinyin: 'dù', meaning: 'belly', explanation: 'Flesh (⺼) + earth = stomach, belly' },\n                { char: '胖', pinyin: 'pàng', meaning: 'fat', explanation: 'Flesh (⺼) + half = plump, overweight' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'As 月: time/celestial. As ⺼: body parts and flesh-related terms.'\n        },\n        '女': {\n            character: '女',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'nǚ',\n            meaning: 'woman, female',\n            etymology: 'Depicts a person in a kneeling position, representing women in ancient society. Now represents femininity and women.',\n            positions: 'Left side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '妈', pinyin: 'mā', meaning: 'mother', explanation: 'Woman (女) + horse (马) = mom (sound-based)' },\n                { char: '她', pinyin: 'tā', meaning: 'she/her', explanation: 'Woman (女) + also = female pronoun \"she\"' },\n                { char: '好', pinyin: 'hǎo', meaning: 'good', explanation: 'Woman (女) + child (子) = mother with child = good' },\n                { char: '姐', pinyin: 'jiě', meaning: 'older sister', explanation: 'Woman (女) + and = older female sibling' },\n                { char: '妹', pinyin: 'mèi', meaning: 'younger sister', explanation: 'Woman (女) + not yet = younger female sibling' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 女 relate to women, female family members, or feminine concepts.'\n        },\n        '言': {\n            character: '言',\n            alternateForms: ['讠'],\n            pinyin: 'yán',\n            meaning: 'speech, words',\n            etymology: 'Shows sound (tongue) coming from mouth. Represents language, speech, and verbal communication. Simplified to 讠 on left side.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 讠, or standalone as 言',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '说', pinyin: 'shuō', meaning: 'to speak', explanation: 'Speech (讠) + exchange = to say, speak' },\n                { char: '话', pinyin: 'huà', meaning: 'speech/words', explanation: 'Speech (讠) + tongue = words, language' },\n                { char: '语', pinyin: 'yǔ', meaning: 'language', explanation: 'Speech (讠) + I/me = language, speech' },\n                { char: '读', pinyin: 'dú', meaning: 'to read', explanation: 'Speech (讠) + sell = to read aloud' },\n                { char: '讲', pinyin: 'jiǎng', meaning: 'to explain', explanation: 'Speech (讠) + well = to explain, teach' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 讠 relate to speaking, language, communication, or verbal expression.'\n        },\n        '食': {\n            character: '食',\n            alternateForms: ['饣', '𩙿'],\n            pinyin: 'shí',\n            meaning: 'food, to eat',\n            etymology: 'Ancient form showed a person over a vessel of food. Represents eating and food-related concepts. Simplified to 饣 on left.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 饣, or standalone as 食',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '饭', pinyin: 'fàn', meaning: 'cooked rice/meal', explanation: 'Food (饣) + counter = cooked rice, meal' },\n                { char: '饿', pinyin: 'è', meaning: 'hungry', explanation: 'Food (饣) + ego/self = hunger, to starve' },\n                { char: '饱', pinyin: 'bǎo', meaning: 'full (from eating)', explanation: 'Food (饣) + embrace = satiated, full' },\n                { char: '饮', pinyin: 'yǐn', meaning: 'to drink', explanation: 'Food (饣) + owe = to drink, beverage' },\n                { char: '馆', pinyin: 'guǎn', meaning: 'restaurant/building', explanation: 'Food (饣) + official = eating establishment' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 饣 relate to food, eating, hunger, or dining activities.'\n        },\n        '金': {\n            character: '金',\n            alternateForms: ['钅'],\n            pinyin: 'jīn',\n            meaning: 'metal, gold',\n            etymology: 'Shows metal ore being mined from earth. Represents metals, minerals, and metallic objects. Simplified to 钅 on left.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 钅, or standalone as 金',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '银', pinyin: 'yín', meaning: 'silver', explanation: 'Metal (钅) + obstinate = silver metal' },\n                { char: '铁', pinyin: 'tiě', meaning: 'iron', explanation: 'Metal (钅) + lost = iron metal' },\n                { char: '钱', pinyin: 'qián', meaning: 'money', explanation: 'Metal (钅) + spade = money (metal coins)' },\n                { char: '钟', pinyin: 'zhōng', meaning: 'clock/bell', explanation: 'Metal (钅) + middle = metal bell or clock' },\n                { char: '铜', pinyin: 'tóng', meaning: 'copper/bronze', explanation: 'Metal (钅) + together = copper metal' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 钅 relate to metals, metallic objects, or mineral substances.'\n        },\n        '火': {\n            character: '火',\n            alternateForms: ['灬', '灭'],\n            pinyin: 'huǒ',\n            meaning: 'fire',\n            etymology: 'Depicts flames rising. Represents fire, heat, and burning. Often appears as four dots (灬) at bottom.',\n            positions: 'Left/right side, bottom as 灬, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '热', pinyin: 'rè', meaning: 'hot', explanation: 'Execute + fire (灬) = heat, hot temperature' },\n                { char: '烧', pinyin: 'shāo', meaning: 'to burn', explanation: 'Fire (火) + yao = to burn, set fire' },\n                { char: '煮', pinyin: 'zhǔ', meaning: 'to cook/boil', explanation: 'Fire (灬) + person + once = to cook with heat' },\n                { char: '烟', pinyin: 'yān', meaning: 'smoke', explanation: 'Fire (火) + western = smoke from fire' },\n                { char: '灯', pinyin: 'dēng', meaning: 'lamp/light', explanation: 'Fire (火) + ascend = lamp, illumination' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 火 or 灬 relate to fire, heat, burning, or cooking.'\n        },\n        '土': {\n            character: '土',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'tǔ',\n            meaning: 'earth, soil',\n            etymology: 'Shows a mound of earth. Represents soil, ground, land, and earthly matters.',\n            positions: 'Left side, bottom, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '地', pinyin: 'dì', meaning: 'earth/ground', explanation: 'Earth (土) + also = land, ground, earth' },\n                { char: '场', pinyin: 'chǎng', meaning: 'field/place', explanation: 'Earth (土) + easy = open area, field' },\n                { char: '城', pinyin: 'chéng', meaning: 'city/wall', explanation: 'Earth (土) + complete = walled city' },\n                { char: '坐', pinyin: 'zuò', meaning: 'to sit', explanation: 'Two people on earth (土) = sitting down' },\n                { char: '块', pinyin: 'kuài', meaning: 'piece/lump', explanation: 'Earth (土) + quick = chunk, piece' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 土 relate to earth, ground, land, or physical locations.'\n        },\n        '竹': {\n            character: '竹',\n            alternateForms: ['⺮'],\n            pinyin: 'zhú',\n            meaning: 'bamboo',\n            etymology: 'Shows two bamboo stalks with leaves. As a radical (⺮), represents bamboo and objects made from bamboo.',\n            positions: 'Top as ⺮, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '笑', pinyin: 'xiào', meaning: 'to laugh', explanation: 'Bamboo (⺮) + young = to laugh (swaying like bamboo)' },\n                { char: '笔', pinyin: 'bǐ', meaning: 'pen/brush', explanation: 'Bamboo (⺮) + hair = writing brush (bamboo handle)' },\n                { char: '算', pinyin: 'suàn', meaning: 'to calculate', explanation: 'Bamboo (⺮) + eye + two = counting with bamboo tallies' },\n                { char: '答', pinyin: 'dá', meaning: 'to answer', explanation: 'Bamboo (⺮) + unite = to respond, answer' },\n                { char: '箱', pinyin: 'xiāng', meaning: 'box/trunk', explanation: 'Bamboo (⺮) + eye = bamboo container, box' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with ⺮ relate to bamboo, bamboo objects, or tools traditionally made from bamboo.'\n        },\n        '艹': {\n            character: '艹',\n            alternateForms: ['草'],\n            pinyin: 'cǎo',\n            meaning: 'grass, plants',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 草 (grass). Shows sprouting plants. Represents vegetation and plant life.',\n            positions: 'Top as ⺾ or 艹',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '花', pinyin: 'huā', meaning: 'flower', explanation: 'Grass (艹) + change = flowers, blooms' },\n                { char: '茶', pinyin: 'chá', meaning: 'tea', explanation: 'Grass (艹) + surplus = tea plant, tea' },\n                { char: '菜', pinyin: 'cài', meaning: 'vegetable/dish', explanation: 'Grass (艹) + pick = vegetables, greens' },\n                { char: '药', pinyin: 'yào', meaning: 'medicine', explanation: 'Grass (艹) + joyful = herbal medicine' },\n                { char: '草', pinyin: 'cǎo', meaning: 'grass', explanation: 'Grass (艹) + early = grass, weeds' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 艹 relate to plants, vegetation, herbs, or botanical items.'\n        },\n        '足': {\n            character: '足',\n            alternateForms: ['𧾷'],\n            pinyin: 'zú',\n            meaning: 'foot, leg',\n            etymology: 'Shows a leg and foot. Represents feet, legs, and movement. As radical, simplified to 𧾷 on left side.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 𧾷, or standalone as 足',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '跑', pinyin: 'pǎo', meaning: 'to run', explanation: 'Foot (𧾷) + wrap = to run, sprint' },\n                { char: '跳', pinyin: 'tiào', meaning: 'to jump', explanation: 'Foot (𧾷) + omen = to jump, leap' },\n                { char: '路', pinyin: 'lù', meaning: 'road', explanation: 'Foot (𧾷) + each = path, road for walking' },\n                { char: '踢', pinyin: 'tī', meaning: 'to kick', explanation: 'Foot (𧾷) + easy = to kick with foot' },\n                { char: '跟', pinyin: 'gēn', meaning: 'heel/to follow', explanation: 'Foot (𧾷) + stubborn = heel, to follow' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 𧾷 relate to feet, legs, walking, or movement with legs.'\n        },\n        '目': {\n            character: '目',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'mù',\n            meaning: 'eye',\n            etymology: 'Depicts an eye turned sideways. Represents eyes, sight, and vision.',\n            positions: 'Left side, standalone, or as component',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '看', pinyin: 'kàn', meaning: 'to look', explanation: 'Hand (手) + eye (目) = to look, watch' },\n                { char: '眼', pinyin: 'yǎn', meaning: 'eye', explanation: 'Eye (目) + good/obstinate = the eye organ' },\n                { char: '睛', pinyin: 'jīng', meaning: 'eyeball/pupil', explanation: 'Eye (目) + blue/green = eyeball, pupil' },\n                { char: '睡', pinyin: 'shuì', meaning: 'to sleep', explanation: 'Eye (目) + hang down = eyes closing, sleep' },\n                { char: '眉', pinyin: 'méi', meaning: 'eyebrow', explanation: 'Eye (目) + below = eyebrows above eyes' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 目 relate to eyes, vision, seeing, or facial expressions.'\n        },\n        '门': {\n            character: '门',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'mén',\n            meaning: 'door, gate',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 門, showing two swinging doors. Represents doors, gates, and entrances.',\n            positions: 'Enclosing other components, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '问', pinyin: 'wèn', meaning: 'to ask', explanation: 'Door (门) + mouth (口) = to inquire at gate' },\n                { char: '开', pinyin: 'kāi', meaning: 'to open', explanation: 'Related to opening doors = to open' },\n                { char: '闭', pinyin: 'bì', meaning: 'to close', explanation: 'Door (门) + talent = to shut, close' },\n                { char: '间', pinyin: 'jiān', meaning: 'between/room', explanation: 'Door (门) + sun = space between, room' },\n                { char: '闻', pinyin: 'wén', meaning: 'to hear/smell', explanation: 'Door (门) + ear = news through door' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 门 relate to doors, openings, spaces, or entry/exit concepts.'\n        },\n        '雨': {\n            character: '雨',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'yǔ',\n            meaning: 'rain',\n            etymology: 'Shows clouds with raindrops falling. Represents rain and weather phenomena.',\n            positions: 'Top, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '雪', pinyin: 'xuě', meaning: 'snow', explanation: 'Rain (雨) + broom/brush = frozen rain, snow' },\n                { char: '雷', pinyin: 'léi', meaning: 'thunder', explanation: 'Rain (雨) + fields = thunder from rainstorm' },\n                { char: '电', pinyin: 'diàn', meaning: 'electricity/lightning', explanation: 'Rain (雨) + bent = lightning in storm' },\n                { char: '云', pinyin: 'yún', meaning: 'cloud', explanation: 'Related to rain (雨) = clouds in sky' },\n                { char: '需', pinyin: 'xū', meaning: 'to need', explanation: 'Rain (雨) + soft = necessity (like rain)' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 雨 relate to weather, precipitation, or atmospheric phenomena.'\n        },\n        '山': {\n            character: '山',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'shān',\n            meaning: 'mountain, hill',\n            etymology: 'Ancient pictograph showing three mountain peaks. Represents mountains, hills, and elevated terrain.',\n            positions: 'Left side, bottom, top, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '岛', pinyin: 'dǎo', meaning: 'island', explanation: 'Mountain (山) + bird = island (mountain in sea)' },\n                { char: '岩', pinyin: 'yán', meaning: 'cliff/rock', explanation: 'Mountain (山) + stone = rocky cliff, crag' },\n                { char: '峰', pinyin: 'fēng', meaning: 'peak/summit', explanation: 'Mountain (山) + high = mountain peak' },\n                { char: '崩', pinyin: 'bēng', meaning: 'collapse', explanation: 'Mountain (山) + friend = mountain collapse' },\n                { char: '岸', pinyin: 'àn', meaning: 'shore/bank', explanation: 'Mountain (山) + cliff = shore, riverbank' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 山 relate to mountains, hills, terrain features, or geological formations.'\n        },\n        '石': {\n            character: '石',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'shí',\n            meaning: 'stone, rock',\n            etymology: 'Shows a stone or boulder under a cliff. Represents stones, rocks, and solid materials.',\n            positions: 'Left side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '砖', pinyin: 'zhuān', meaning: 'brick', explanation: 'Stone (石) + exclusive = brick (processed stone)' },\n                { char: '破', pinyin: 'pò', meaning: 'broken', explanation: 'Stone (石) + skin = to break, smash' },\n                { char: '硬', pinyin: 'yìng', meaning: 'hard', explanation: 'Stone (石) + more = hard, solid (like stone)' },\n                { char: '矿', pinyin: 'kuàng', meaning: 'ore/mine', explanation: 'Stone (石) + wide = mineral ore, mine' },\n                { char: '码', pinyin: 'mǎ', meaning: 'number/code', explanation: 'Stone (石) + horse = code, number (counting stones)' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 石 relate to stones, rocks, minerals, or hard solid objects.'\n        },\n        '田': {\n            character: '田',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'tián',\n            meaning: 'field, farmland',\n            etymology: 'Depicts a grid of agricultural fields from above. Represents farmland, fields, and agriculture.',\n            positions: 'Standalone or as component',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '男', pinyin: 'nán', meaning: 'male/man', explanation: 'Field (田) + strength (力) = man working in field' },\n                { char: '思', pinyin: 'sī', meaning: 'to think', explanation: 'Field (田) + heart = thoughts organized like fields' },\n                { char: '畜', pinyin: 'chù', meaning: 'livestock', explanation: 'Field (田) + animal = farm animals, livestock' },\n                { char: '界', pinyin: 'jiè', meaning: 'boundary', explanation: 'Field (田) + divide = boundary, border' },\n                { char: '留', pinyin: 'liú', meaning: 'to stay', explanation: 'Field (田) + stem = to remain, keep' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 田 relate to fields, agriculture, organization, or grid-like structures.'\n        },\n        '车': {\n            character: '车',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'chē',\n            meaning: 'vehicle, cart',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 車, showing a cart viewed from above with wheels and axle. Represents vehicles and wheeled transport.',\n            positions: 'Left side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '轮', pinyin: 'lún', meaning: 'wheel', explanation: 'Vehicle (车) + book/册 = wheel, rotation' },\n                { char: '轻', pinyin: 'qīng', meaning: 'light/gentle', explanation: 'Vehicle (车) + labor = light (easy to move)' },\n                { char: '软', pinyin: 'ruǎn', meaning: 'soft', explanation: 'Vehicle (车) + lacking = soft, flexible' },\n                { char: '转', pinyin: 'zhuǎn', meaning: 'to turn', explanation: 'Vehicle (车) + special = to rotate, turn' },\n                { char: '载', pinyin: 'zài', meaning: 'to carry', explanation: 'Vehicle (车) + [load] = to transport, carry' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 车 relate to vehicles, transportation, wheels, or movement.'\n        },\n        '马': {\n            character: '马',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'mǎ',\n            meaning: 'horse',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 馬, ancient pictograph of a horse with flowing mane. Represents horses and equine-related concepts.',\n            positions: 'Left side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '骑', pinyin: 'qí', meaning: 'to ride', explanation: 'Horse (马) + strange = to ride (horse)' },\n                { char: '驾', pinyin: 'jià', meaning: 'to drive', explanation: 'Horse (马) + add = to drive, control' },\n                { char: '驶', pinyin: 'shǐ', meaning: 'to sail/drive', explanation: 'Horse (马) + history = to drive (vehicle)' },\n                { char: '验', pinyin: 'yàn', meaning: 'to test', explanation: 'Horse (马) + test = to examine, verify' },\n                { char: '骗', pinyin: 'piàn', meaning: 'to cheat', explanation: 'Horse (马) + flat = to deceive, trick' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 马 relate to horses, riding, movement, or speed-related actions.'\n        },\n        '鱼': {\n            character: '鱼',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'yú',\n            meaning: 'fish',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 魚, ancient pictograph showing fish with head, body, and tail. Represents fish and aquatic life.',\n            positions: 'Left side, bottom, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '鲜', pinyin: 'xiān', meaning: 'fresh', explanation: 'Fish (鱼) + sheep = fresh (fresh fish)' },\n                { char: '鲨', pinyin: 'shā', meaning: 'shark', explanation: 'Fish (鱼) + sand = shark fish' },\n                { char: '鲸', pinyin: 'jīng', meaning: 'whale', explanation: 'Fish (鱼) + capital = whale (large fish)' },\n                { char: '鳞', pinyin: 'lín', meaning: 'scales', explanation: 'Fish (鱼) + neighboring = fish scales' },\n                { char: '鲤', pinyin: 'lǐ', meaning: 'carp', explanation: 'Fish (鱼) + village = carp fish' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 鱼 relate to fish, aquatic animals, or seafood.'\n        },\n        '鸟': {\n            character: '鸟',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'niǎo',\n            meaning: 'bird',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 鳥, ancient pictograph of a bird with beak, body, and tail feathers. Represents birds and avian creatures.',\n            positions: 'Right side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '鸡', pinyin: 'jī', meaning: 'chicken', explanation: 'Another + bird (鸟) = chicken, domestic fowl' },\n                { char: '鸭', pinyin: 'yā', meaning: 'duck', explanation: 'Armor + bird (鸟) = duck waterfowl' },\n                { char: '鹅', pinyin: 'é', meaning: 'goose', explanation: 'Me/self + bird (鸟) = goose' },\n                { char: '鹰', pinyin: 'yīng', meaning: 'eagle/hawk', explanation: 'Respond + bird (鸟) = eagle, hawk' },\n                { char: '鸽', pinyin: 'gē', meaning: 'pigeon', explanation: 'Unity + bird (鸟) = pigeon, dove' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 鸟 relate to birds, avian species, or flying creatures.'\n        },\n        '犬': {\n            character: '犬',\n            alternateForms: ['犭'],\n            pinyin: 'quǎn',\n            meaning: 'dog',\n            etymology: 'Pictograph of a dog standing in profile. As a radical (犭), represents dogs and animals. Related to animalistic qualities.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 犭, or standalone as 犬',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '猫', pinyin: 'māo', meaning: 'cat', explanation: 'Dog (犭) + sprout = cat (feline animal)' },\n                { char: '狗', pinyin: 'gǒu', meaning: 'dog', explanation: 'Dog (犭) + sentence = dog, canine' },\n                { char: '猪', pinyin: 'zhū', meaning: 'pig', explanation: 'Dog (犭) + person = pig (farm animal)' },\n                { char: '狼', pinyin: 'láng', meaning: 'wolf', explanation: 'Dog (犭) + good/obstinate = wolf (wild canine)' },\n                { char: '猴', pinyin: 'hóu', meaning: 'monkey', explanation: 'Dog (犭) + marquis = monkey (wild animal)' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 犭 relate to animals, mammals, or wild creatures.'\n        },\n        '刀': {\n            character: '刀',\n            alternateForms: ['刂'],\n            pinyin: 'dāo',\n            meaning: 'knife, blade',\n            etymology: 'Depicts a curved blade. As radical (刂) on right, represents cutting, dividing, or sharp actions.',\n            positions: 'Right side as 刂, or standalone as 刀',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '刻', pinyin: 'kè', meaning: 'to carve', explanation: 'Engrave + knife (刂) = to carve, engrave' },\n                { char: '切', pinyin: 'qiē', meaning: 'to cut', explanation: 'Seven + knife (刀) = to cut, slice' },\n                { char: '分', pinyin: 'fēn', meaning: 'to divide', explanation: 'Eight + knife (刂) = to separate, divide' },\n                { char: '刚', pinyin: 'gāng', meaning: 'just now/hard', explanation: 'Net/square + knife (刂) = just, firm' },\n                { char: '到', pinyin: 'dào', meaning: 'to arrive', explanation: 'Arrive + knife (刂) = to reach, arrive at' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 刂 or 刀 relate to cutting, dividing, arriving, or decisive actions.'\n        },\n        '力': {\n            character: '力',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'lì',\n            meaning: 'strength, power',\n            etymology: 'Depicts a muscular arm or flexed bicep. Represents physical strength, power, and effort.',\n            positions: 'Right side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '加', pinyin: 'jiā', meaning: 'to add', explanation: 'Force + strength (力) = to add, increase' },\n                { char: '功', pinyin: 'gōng', meaning: 'merit/success', explanation: 'Work + strength (力) = achievement, merit' },\n                { char: '助', pinyin: 'zhù', meaning: 'to help', explanation: 'Moreover + strength (力) = to assist, help' },\n                { char: '动', pinyin: 'dòng', meaning: 'to move', explanation: 'Heavy + strength (力) = to move, motion' },\n                { char: '劳', pinyin: 'láo', meaning: 'to toil', explanation: 'Fire + grass + strength (力) = labor, toil' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 力 relate to strength, effort, work, or physical exertion.'\n        },\n        '耳': {\n            character: '耳',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'ěr',\n            meaning: 'ear',\n            etymology: 'Pictograph showing the shape of a human ear. Represents hearing, listening, and ears.',\n            positions: 'Left side, right side, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '听', pinyin: 'tīng', meaning: 'to listen', explanation: 'Mouth (口) + ear (耳) = to listen, hear' },\n                { char: '闻', pinyin: 'wén', meaning: 'to hear/smell', explanation: 'Door (门) + ear (耳) = to hear news' },\n                { char: '聪', pinyin: 'cōng', meaning: 'smart/clever', explanation: 'Ear (耳) + multiple = intelligent (good listener)' },\n                { char: '职', pinyin: 'zhí', meaning: 'duty/job', explanation: 'Ear (耳) + sound = responsibility, job' },\n                { char: '联', pinyin: 'lián', meaning: 'to connect', explanation: 'Ear (耳) + thread = to connect, link' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 耳 relate to hearing, ears, listening, or communication.'\n        },\n        '虫': {\n            character: '虫',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'chóng',\n            meaning: 'insect, bug',\n            etymology: 'Depicts a coiled snake or insect. Represents insects, bugs, and small creatures.',\n            positions: 'Left side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '蚊', pinyin: 'wén', meaning: 'mosquito', explanation: 'Insect (虫) + script = mosquito (biting bug)' },\n                { char: '蛇', pinyin: 'shé', meaning: 'snake', explanation: 'Insect (虫) + it/other = snake, serpent' },\n                { char: '蜜', pinyin: 'mì', meaning: 'honey', explanation: 'Insect (虫) + must/necessary = honey (from bees)' },\n                { char: '蝴', pinyin: 'hú', meaning: 'butterfly', explanation: 'Insect (虫) + beard = butterfly (蝴蝶)' },\n                { char: '蚂', pinyin: 'mǎ', meaning: 'ant', explanation: 'Insect (虫) + horse = ant (蚂蚁)' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 虫 relate to insects, bugs, reptiles, or small creatures.'\n        },\n        '衣': {\n            character: '衣',\n            alternateForms: ['衤'],\n            pinyin: 'yī',\n            meaning: 'clothing, garment',\n            etymology: 'Shows a robe or garment with sleeves. As radical (衤), represents clothing, fabric, and wearing.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 衤, or standalone as 衣',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '裤', pinyin: 'kù', meaning: 'pants', explanation: 'Clothing (衤) + warehouse = pants, trousers' },\n                { char: '袖', pinyin: 'xiù', meaning: 'sleeve', explanation: 'Clothing (衤) + from/by = sleeve of garment' },\n                { char: '被', pinyin: 'bèi', meaning: 'quilt/by', explanation: 'Clothing (衤) + skin = blanket, quilt' },\n                { char: '补', pinyin: 'bǔ', meaning: 'to mend', explanation: 'Clothing (衤) + plant = to mend clothes' },\n                { char: '初', pinyin: 'chū', meaning: 'beginning', explanation: 'Clothing (衤) + knife = first (cutting new cloth)' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 衤 relate to clothing, fabric, garments, or wearing.'\n        },\n        '贝': {\n            character: '贝',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'bèi',\n            meaning: 'shell, money',\n            etymology: 'Shows a cowrie shell used as ancient currency. Represents money, value, and trade.',\n            positions: 'Left side, bottom, or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '财', pinyin: 'cái', meaning: 'wealth', explanation: 'Talent + shell (贝) = wealth, riches' },\n                { char: '购', pinyin: 'gòu', meaning: 'to buy', explanation: 'Net/structure + shell (贝) = to purchase' },\n                { char: '贵', pinyin: 'guì', meaning: 'expensive', explanation: 'Returning + shell (贝) = expensive, precious' },\n                { char: '贷', pinyin: 'dài', meaning: 'to lend', explanation: 'Substitute + shell (贝) = to loan, lend' },\n                { char: '货', pinyin: 'huò', meaning: 'goods', explanation: 'Transform + shell (贝) = goods, merchandise' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 贝 relate to money, commerce, value, or financial transactions.'\n        },\n        '走': {\n            character: '走',\n            alternateForms: ['辶'],\n            pinyin: 'zǒu',\n            meaning: 'to walk, go',\n            etymology: 'Shows a person walking. As radical (辶), represents movement, travel, and roads.',\n            positions: 'Bottom/left as 辶, or standalone as 走',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '近', pinyin: 'jìn', meaning: 'near', explanation: 'Axe + walk (辶) = near, close (short walk)' },\n                { char: '远', pinyin: 'yuǎn', meaning: 'far', explanation: 'Distant + walk (辶) = far, distant' },\n                { char: '进', pinyin: 'jìn', meaning: 'to enter', explanation: 'Well + walk (辶) = to advance, enter' },\n                { char: '还', pinyin: 'huán', meaning: 'to return', explanation: 'Not yet + walk (辶) = to return, still' },\n                { char: '过', pinyin: 'guò', meaning: 'to pass', explanation: 'Bone + walk (辶) = to pass by, cross' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 辶 relate to walking, movement, travel, or roads.'\n        },\n        '酉': {\n            character: '酉',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'yǒu',\n            meaning: 'alcohol, wine',\n            etymology: 'Shows an ancient wine jar or fermentation vessel. Represents alcohol, brewing, and fermentation.',\n            positions: 'Right side or standalone',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '酒', pinyin: 'jiǔ', meaning: 'alcohol/wine', explanation: 'Water (氵) + wine vessel (酉) = alcohol, liquor' },\n                { char: '醉', pinyin: 'zuì', meaning: 'drunk', explanation: 'Soldier + wine (酉) = intoxicated, drunk' },\n                { char: '酸', pinyin: 'suān', meaning: 'sour', explanation: 'Ancestral + wine (酉) = sour (fermented taste)' },\n                { char: '醋', pinyin: 'cù', meaning: 'vinegar', explanation: 'Past + wine (酉) = vinegar (soured wine)' },\n                { char: '酷', pinyin: 'kù', meaning: 'cruel/cool', explanation: 'Announce + wine (酉) = harsh, cool' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 酉 relate to alcohol, fermentation, beverages, or taste.'\n        },\n        '彳': {\n            character: '彳',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'chì',\n            meaning: 'step, stride',\n            etymology: 'Shows the left half of the character 行 (to go). Represents walking, stepping, and movement.',\n            positions: 'Left side only',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '行', pinyin: 'xíng', meaning: 'to walk/go', explanation: 'Step (彳) + step (亍) = to go, walk' },\n                { char: '街', pinyin: 'jiē', meaning: 'street', explanation: 'Step (彳) + main + earth = street, road' },\n                { char: '很', pinyin: 'hěn', meaning: 'very', explanation: 'Step (彳) + stubborn = very (emphasis)' },\n                { char: '往', pinyin: 'wǎng', meaning: 'toward', explanation: 'Step (彳) + king = to go toward' },\n                { char: '待', pinyin: 'dài', meaning: 'to wait', explanation: 'Step (彳) + temple = to wait, treat' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 彳 relate to walking, streets, movement, or actions involving steps.'\n        },\n        '冫': {\n            character: '冫',\n            alternateForms: [],\n            pinyin: 'bīng',\n            meaning: 'ice',\n            etymology: 'Two short strokes representing ice crystals or frozen water. Represents coldness and ice.',\n            positions: 'Left side only',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '冷', pinyin: 'lěng', meaning: 'cold', explanation: 'Ice (冫) + command = cold temperature' },\n                { char: '冰', pinyin: 'bīng', meaning: 'ice', explanation: 'Ice (冫) + water (水) = frozen water, ice' },\n                { char: '冻', pinyin: 'dòng', meaning: 'to freeze', explanation: 'Ice (冫) + east = to freeze solid' },\n                { char: '凉', pinyin: 'liáng', meaning: 'cool', explanation: 'Ice (冫) + capital = cool, refreshing' },\n                { char: '准', pinyin: 'zhǔn', meaning: 'accurate', explanation: 'Ice (冫) + nest = standard, precise' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 冫 relate to ice, cold, coolness, or frozen states.'\n        },\n        '纟': {\n            character: '纟',\n            alternateForms: ['糸'],\n            pinyin: 'sī',\n            meaning: 'silk, thread',\n            etymology: 'Simplified from 糸, showing twisted silk threads. Represents textiles, thread, and connection.',\n            positions: 'Left side as 纟',\n            examples: [\n                { char: '红', pinyin: 'hóng', meaning: 'red', explanation: 'Thread (纟) + work = red (dyed thread)' },\n                { char: '级', pinyin: 'jí', meaning: 'grade/level', explanation: 'Thread (纟) + reach = rank, level' },\n                { char: '纸', pinyin: 'zhǐ', meaning: 'paper', explanation: 'Thread (纟) + family = paper (from pulp)' },\n                { char: '线', pinyin: 'xiàn', meaning: 'thread/line', explanation: 'Thread (纟) + spring = thread, wire' },\n                { char: '给', pinyin: 'gěi', meaning: 'to give', explanation: 'Thread (纟) + unite = to give, provide' }\n            ],\n            commonPatterns: 'Characters with 纟 relate to thread, fabric, textiles, or things that connect.'\n        }\n    };\n\n    // Vocabulary data organized by category\n    const vocabularyData = {\n        numbers: {\n            title: 'Numbers (0-100)',\n            icon: 'calculator',\n            items: [\n                { character: '零', pinyin: 'líng', meaning: '0 (zero)' },\n                { character: '一', pinyin: 'yī', meaning: '1 (one)' },\n                { character: '二', pinyin: 'èr', meaning: '2 (two)' },\n                { character: '三', pinyin: 'sān', meaning: '3 (three)' },\n                { character: '四', pinyin: 'sì', meaning: '4 (four)' },\n                { character: '五', pinyin: 'wǔ', meaning: '5 (five)' },\n                { character: '六', pinyin: 'liù', meaning: '6 (six)' },\n                { character: '七', pinyin: 'qī', meaning: '7 (seven)' },\n                { character: '八', pinyin: 'bā', meaning: '8 (eight)' },\n                { character: '九', pinyin: 'jiǔ', meaning: '9 (nine)' },\n                { character: '十', pinyin: 'shí', meaning: '10 (ten)' },\n                { character: '二十', pinyin: 'èrshí',